5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":16,"verse":19,"english":"He was inflamed with amour, pride and haughtiness and his expansive eyes were coppery and idle. And he appeared like Cupid himself just appearing in view, leaving behind his bow and arrows.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-18-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5016019","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b45fa36fae4ea3f532614bf4e61ea26d3367296325476a4228fc3957b55392ac","compact":"6c291b9089f254afcca8b016e9746b822c414cb3ad6598bbbe36e9a4e5142981","nasal":"f71aa7028dc58af6999eff593c5daa5a07e8b3cd82ef1a88bce43a9ef20e2faa"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-16-20","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":16,"verse":20,"english":"Holding his excellent robe, covered with flowers, washed, set with jewels and white as the foam of the churned nectar, he placed it in its proper place.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.772,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-18-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5016020","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"08ead6d7f3fec4dcc8d2bf598c3801c9ccdb957c2a66ddc9d4f8118ffc7ca784","compact":"54698d986472167a6335891484fb0ba34748bbd6b2546d297f7885273fa297b0","nasal":"77534dc912450808e2b38e3f94f4f276df8ce023012ccb5448406d09d13ab829"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-16-21","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":16,"verse":21,"english":"Hanumăn, hiding himself on the tree, in the midst of many leaves and flowers, tried to recognise him as he approached.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.638,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-18-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5016021","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"62c8e81a8a8e850cca461e7017bdf649fb28582727d522d26ba145ed945020eb","compac